# P30: Package manager manifest — apt/dpkg (Debian/Ubuntu)
Source: ix
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: savageops <noreply@savageops.com>
Build-Depends: zig (>= 0.16.0)
Standards-Version: 4.5.0

Package: ix
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6
Description: A search engine that knows what to ignore
 IX classifies each query at parse time and routes it to the narrowest
 execution path before touching a byte of input. Literal queries hit
 256-bit SIMD lanes at 32 bytes per cycle. Regex compiles through PCRE2
 JIT. AND/OR queries extract mandatory trigram evidence and reject
 ineligible files before scanning.
 .
 Features:
  * AVX2 SIMD literal scan (32 bytes/cycle)
  * Trigram-gated file rejection (sub-linear pruning)
  * Warm index with persistent trigram postings
  * BM25 degree-of-interest context assembly (xo)
  * Cursor-paginated, byte-budgeted agent output
  * MCP server for agent-native integration
  * Shell completions for bash/zsh/fish/PowerShell
  * Single static binary, zero runtime dependencies
